+// How much of the GEMM result this op keeps in flight, in FLOATS. The result is `K/s0` times the size
+// of dst if computed whole, so it is blocked over input positions and this is the block's budget --
+// 256 KB, chosen to sit inside a small shared L2 alongside the two operands. Reserved by
+// ggml_graph_plan (see GGML_OP_CONV_TRANSPOSE_1D there), so the two must agree.
+#define GGML_CONV_TRANSPOSE_1D_TILE (64*1024)
+
+// A SKEW BETWEEN THE TWO PANELS THIS OP PACKS, in FLOATS, and it is worth 3.5x on one of a VITS
+// vocoder's three conv_transpose_1d nodes.
+//
+// The kernel goes to `wdata` and the transposed activation to `wdata + nk`, and the GEMM then walks
+// both with lda = ldb = k. Its 4x4 tile has eight live streams -- four rows of each operand, k floats
+// apart -- so whenever `nk` is a whole number of cache ways the a-streams and the b-streams land in
+// the SAME SETS, four ways deep, and evict each other on every access. That is not a rare alignment:
+// `nk` is K*Cout*Cin, and the node this was found on has nk = 524288 floats, exactly 2 MB. The
+// panels are placed on top of each other by construction.
+//
+// Measured on a Pi Zero W (16 KB 4-way L1, so a 4 KB way) at that node's shape, m=2048 k=256 n=64,
+// gemm44 in isolation, two passes (loom `scripts/bench37.c`):
+//
+//     panels adjacent, as before          82.1 / 81.7 MMAC/s
+//     +4 floats                          200.8 / 200.4
+//     +8 floats  (one 32-byte line)      283.4 / 236.4     <- works, but not stably
+//     +16 floats (two lines)             286.4 / 285.6     <- this
+//
+// Sixteen rather than eight because eight is one line and lands differently depending on where the
+// work buffer itself starts. THE OTHER OBVIOUS FIX DOES NOT WORK, and it is worth recording: blocking
+// the k loop so the live window is smaller changes nothing at all (81.7 at KB=128, 83.1 at KB=64),
+// which is what says this is a set conflict rather than a capacity miss. Padding lda/ldb instead
+// works equally well (up to 284.8) and costs a stride parameter through ggml_call_mul_mat_ldc; this
+// costs one addend.
+//
+// Reserved by ggml_graph_plan alongside the tile above, so the two must agree.
+#define GGML_CONV_TRANSPOSE_1D_SKEW 16
 void ggml_compute_forward_conv_transpose_1d(const struct ggml_compute_params * params, struct ggml_tensor * dst);
